      "content": "interesting. you mentioned the \"mist and goblins\" thing as an example of labeling a swamp. \n\ni guess my concern is about the tone of the catalog. if i start using descriptive terms like \"unidentified entity\" or \"legendary creature\" in the metadata, will that make the collection look unprofessional or unscholarly to other researchers? how do i balance these descriptions so they are useful for identification without making the archive look like it's leaning into fantasy?",
